                            {
                                "id": "AID-E-003.005",
                                "comparison": "AID-E-003.005 evicts compromised adapters and derivatives; AID-R-001.001 restores and verifies known-good model or adapter state.\nAID-R-001.001 consumes quarantine and tombstone evidence but owns only the rollback and live-release verification. A restored deployment does not prove incident-time adapter eviction across serving, registries, caches, and lineage."
                            }
